e-state/` tree. If that flag was dropped, the stage\n43\t   reads a path relative to `certcomp/` and silently finds nothing — this is the\n44\t   exact failure mode the 2026-04-22 executor change was made to fix.\n45\t3. **Chapter-number mismatch.** This prompt is headed \"Chapter 4\", but the\n46\t   cached sources are heavily annotated for Chapters 1, 2, and 3 (§-level\n47\t   drafting notes for ch01/ch02/ch03, `ch02-fig02`/`ch02-fig04`/`ch03-fig03`\n48\t   anchors, Chapter 3 open questions #8/#9). No snapshot carries Chapter 4\n49\t   scoping notes. It is worth confirming that a Chapter 4 draft exists at all\n50\t   before assuming a read failure.\n51\t\n52\t## Required before re-running Stage 6\n53\t\n54\t1. Confirm the draft exists on disk:\n55\t   `ls ../Book-KCNA/.pipeline-state/ch-04/draft-v2.md` (and `draft-voice.md`).\n56\t2. If absent, check for a live or crashed upstream stage:\n57\t   `cat ../Book-KCNA/.pipeline-state/ch-04/.draft-v2.md.heartbeat`\n58\t   `tail -50 ../Book-KCNA/.pipeline-state/ch-04/.draft-v2.md.progress.log`\n59\t3. If present on disk but not delivered to this stage, verify the executor's\n60\t   `--add-dir` argument covers the book's pipeline-state tree.\n61\t4. Re-run Stage 6 once the draft materializes. The cached-source block is intact\n62\t   and sufficient to audit; only the draft is missing.\n63\t\n64\t## Notes for the re-run (carried forward, not findings)\n65\t\n66\tThese are known hazards in the cache that the eventual Chapter 4 audit should\n67\tapply. They are recorded here so the information isn't lost to a failed stage;\n68\tnone of them is a finding against a draft.\n69\t\n70\t- **Do not accept \"60 questions\" as sourced.** `provenance-kcna-60-questions-2026-08-23.md`\n71\t  is explicitly marked NOT AUTHORITATIVE. The count is absent from every\n72\t  authoritative LF/CNCF source checked.\n73\t- **Passing score phrasing is constrained.** Only\n74\t  \"The Linux Foundation publishes a 75% passing standard for its multipl